---
// /leicht — a light study of the whole product in one route.
//
// The site knows a lot and says all of it: /uebungen/grammatik lists 28 topic cards under
// five level headings, the Wortschatz trainer opens on a deck of 3.375 words with tabs,
// language switches and a picker around it, and the dashboard reports six skills at once.
// On a 390px phone — which is who this is for — none of that fits, and a learner who
// cannot see the end of a screen decides they cannot do the thing on it.
//
// So this route rebuilds the same product under four rules and nothing else:
//
//   1. One decision per screen, three options at the very most.
//   2. A sitting, not a pile. Nothing states a total — no 3.375, no 28, no 412.
//   3. Progress is a sentence you can feel ("Du fragst nach dem Weg."), not a percentage.
//   4. One primary action, in the thumb zone, always.
//
// It is deliberately content-free: three sittings of five tasks, hardcoded in
// src/lib/leicht-app.js. It imports nothing from src/data and writes to its own
// localStorage key, so running it can neither slow down nor disturb the real site. What
// is being tested here is the shape of the flow; if it wins, the shape gets rebuilt
// against the real catalogue, and nothing in these three files is meant to survive that.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/leicht.css";
---
<Layout
  title="Leicht – UX-Prototyp – DeutschAcademy"
  description="Interner Prototyp: der Lernfluss auf das Nötigste reduziert."
>
  <div id="lt-app" class="lt-app">
    <noscript>
      <p style="padding:24px">Dieser Prototyp braucht JavaScript — er ist eine Studie zum Ablauf, keine Seite zum Lesen.</p>
    </noscript>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { mountLeicht } from "../lib/leicht-view.js";
  mountLeicht(document.getElementById("lt-app"));
</script>

<style is:global>
  /* The prototype owns the viewport: no page scroll, no site chrome above it. Scoped to
     this route by the attribute the page sets on <html> below. */
  html[data-leicht],
  html[data-leicht] body {
    overflow: hidden;
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  document.documentElement.dataset.leicht = "";
</script>
